      {
        "name": "Try-With-Resources for Clients",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "BlobServiceClient and BlobServiceAsyncClient are created but never closed. No try-with-resources or finally blocks for client lifecycle management in Main.java."
      },
      {
        "name": "Configures custom retry policy (exponential backoff, max retries, delay)",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Attempts to use ExponentialBackoffOptions with setMaxRetries/setBaseDelay/setMaxDelay, but passes it directly to retryOptions() which expects RetryOptions — code won't compile. Intent is correct but implementation is broken."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sets per-request or per-operation timeout",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "The createTimeoutPolicy() method is a complete no-op — it reads requestTimeout from context but does nothing with it. The NettyAsyncHttpClientBuilder.responseTimeout() would work but the dependency is missing from pom.xml."
      },
      {
        "name": "Enables HTTP logging (HttpLogOptions)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "HttpLogOptions is properly configured with a configurable HttpLogDetailLevel and passed to the client builder."
      },
      {
        "name": "Implements blob lease acquisition before overwrite",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses BlobLeaseClientBuilder to create lease clients, acquireLease() and releaseLease() are implemented. Upload with lease uses BlobRequestConditions.setLeaseId(). Demo acquires lease before overwrite."
      },
      {
        "name": "Implements parallel/block upload for large files (ParallelTransferOptions)",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Uses BlobParallelUploadOptions with setBlockSizeLong but does not configure ParallelTransferOptions (maxConcurrency, maxSingleUploadSize). The async version manually chunks files with Stream.generate() which is exactly the manual chunking the criterion prohibits."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sets blob index tags on upload",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Both sync and async upload methods accept Map\u003cString, String\u003e tags and call .setTags(tags) on BlobParallelUploadOptions."
      },
      {
        "name": "Properly composes reactive chains in the demo",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Async demo in Main.java calls .block() after each individual operation sequentially. No reactive chain composition — each operation is independently subscribed and blocked. Should compose operations with .then()/.flatMap() before a single terminal .block()."
      }
    ]
  },
